Thurea — harmful-site blocker managed by the system

What it does
  /etc/hosts            64,000+ harmful domains pointed nowhere (your own lines are kept)
  systemd-resolved      Cloudflare for Families DNS (harmful content filtered)
  Chromium, Chrome, Brave, Edge, Vivaldi
                        Thurea force-installed (can't be disabled or removed), family DNS
                        inside the browser, Google SafeSearch, YouTube safe filter (no Restricted Mode),
                        no incognito or guest windows
  network (nftables)    only the system resolver may send DNS; other apps can't use DNS-over-TLS or
                        public DNS-over-HTTPS servers (so browsers like Ladybird stay on family DNS)
  Firefox family        family DNS locked on, private browsing off, known harmful sites blocked
  pacman                removing thurea is refused; Tor Browser, Mullvad Browser and
                        Opera can't be installed; everything is re-applied after every
                        transaction
  systemd               re-applied at boot, every 5 minutes and whenever a guarded file changes;
                        guarded files are made immutable (chattr +i)

Updating Thurea: rebuild with build.sh in the source folder, then `sudo pacman -U` the new package.
